<description>
Part of https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/issues/32093

Returning feerates in BTC/kvB it can be very burdensome and is not good practice, as the most widely adopted units are sat/vB.

The RPC affectd by this PR are `getmempoolinfo`, `getnetworkinfo`, `getwalletinfo`, `estimatesmartfee` and `estimaterawfee`.

Because of sub 1sat/vB environment we cannot rely on GetFee() because it internally uses FeeFrac EvaluateFee() function which rounds the values to always return an int. If the `feerate < 1` then it will be rounded to 1 or 0.

For more context or discuss how to migrate also arguments please refer to the open issue https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/issues/32093.
</description>

<commits>
af05ed05f4 rpc: Add ValueFromFeeRate function to core_write

Similar to ValueFromAmount this function returns a UniValue object with the feerate given a CFeeRate object.

c553c8d8b5 test: add unit tests for ValueFromFeeRate

d72ba2a2e2 rpc: let MempoolInfoToJSON to return feerates in sat/vb

This commit also includes mempool.h, which was missing and was causing function definition issues.

eee1a05ddf rpc: allow getmempoolinfo to return feerates in sat/vb

84e8ddc34c rpc: allow getnetworkinfo to return feerates in sat/vb

4ae601310c rpc: allow named options in estimatesmartfee

Accept fee_rate_estimator and verbosity as top-level named arguments while preserving the third-position options object and existing defaults.

542e7ac27a rpc: allow estimatesmartfee to return feerates in sat/vb

e345ecd721 rpc: allow estimaterawfee to return feerates in sat/vB

Co-authored-by: w0xlt <woltx@protonmail.com>

